From: Wine Debugging Session
Subject: [PATCH] imm32: Fix WM_IME_CONTROL stub to return 0 instead of 1.

The WM_IME_CONTROL stub in ime_ui_window_proc returns 1 for all
sub-commands, but IMC_CLOSESTATUSWINDOW should return 0 (matching
Windows behavior when there is no status window to close).

This fixes "SendMessage() error" in the DAL5 visual novel engine
(e.g. Date A Live: Ren Dystopia) which checks the return value
of SendMessage(WM_IME_CONTROL, IMC_CLOSESTATUSWINDOW) and expects 0.

Backported from Proton's Wine fork.

diff --git a/dlls/imm32/ime.c b/dlls/imm32/ime.c
--- a/dlls/imm32/ime.c
+++ b/dlls/imm32/ime.c
@@ -464,7 +464,7 @@
     case WM_IME_CONTROL:
         FIXME( "hwnd %p, himc %p, msg %s, wparam %s, lparam %#Ix stub!\n", hwnd, himc,
                debugstr_wm_ime(msg), debugstr_imc(wparam), lparam );
-        return 1;
+        return 0;
     }
 
     return DefWindowProcW( hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam );
